title: 'Polkadot: Verify the workers at startup'
doc:
- audience:
  - Node Dev
  - Node Operator
  description: "# Description\n\nCloses #8117\n\nToday, `polkadot` checks that its\
    \ PVF workers are running the same version at startup, but the workers' other\
    \ security checks (landlock, seccomp, unshare/change-root, clone, etc.) only run\
    \ when a worker is actually spawned. If the node is not yet part of the active\
    \ validator set, an operator running a misconfigured or under-sandboxed worker\
    \ has no way to find out \u2014 until the node starts validating, loses rewards,\
    \ and degrades the network.\n\nThis PR runs those checks at startup too, the same\
    \ way the version check already does: `polkadot` invokes `execute-worker --check-security-features\
    \ --worker-dir-path <workers-path>` once before the node starts, and refuses to\
    \ start if the worker binary is missing or fails its security checks. This way\
    \ operators are informed immediately, rather than only once the node is selected\
    \ as a validator.\n\n## Integration\n\nNode operators who pass `--workers-path`\
    \ will now have their `execute-worker binary's security checks verified once at\
    \ startup, before the node starts:\n\n- If the worker binary is missing or cannot\
    \ be spawned, the node now fails to start with `Error::ExecuteWorkerSpawnFailed`\
    \ (binary path + underlying IO error), instead of panicking.\n- If the worker\
    \ reports failed security checks, the node fails to start with `Error::ExecuteWorkerFailedSecurityChecks`\
    \ (binary path + worker dir path).\n\nNo changes to the normal worker spawn/handshake\
    \ path (`polkadot-node-core-pvf`' `spawn_with_program_path`/`with_transient_socket_path`)\
    \ \u2014 that continues to work exactly as before.\n\n`polkadot-node-core-pvf-common::worker::check_security_status`\
    \ is a new `pub fn`, used internally by the `decl_worker_main!` macro for the\
    \ `--check-security-features` flag.\n\n## Review Notes\n\n- `polkadot/cli/src/command.rs`:\
    \ new `verify_workers_security_checks` runs `<workers_path>/execute-worker --check-security-features\
    \ --worker-dir-path <workers_path>` and maps a non-zero exit status / spawn failure\
    \ to the new `Error` variants. It's called from `run()` right after CLI args are\
    \ parsed, before any service/runner setup.\n- `polkadot/node/core/pvf/common/src/worker/mod.rs`:\n\
    \  - New `check_security_status(worker_kind, worker_dir_path) -> bool`: checks\
    \ that the worker dir is readable and, on Linux, best-effort probes landlock/seccomp/change-root/clone\
    \ \u2014 all logged as warnings and non-fatal, mirroring the best-effort philosophy\
    \ already used for `SecurityStatus`.\n  - `decl_worker_main!`'s argument parsing\
    \ was reordered so `--worker-dir-path` is resolved (and the `do_security_checks`\
    \ early exit can happen) before `--socket-path` is required, since the standalone\
    \ check is never given a socket path.\n- `polkadot/cli/src/error.rs`: added `ExecuteWorkerFailedSecurityChecks`\
    \ and `ExecuteWorkerSpawnFailed` variants.\n- Tests added:\n  - `polkadot/cli/src/command.rs`:\
    \ unit tests for `verify_workers_security_checks` covering success, worker-reported\
    \ failure, missing binary, and the exact argument order, using stub shell-script\
    \ \"workers\".\n  - `polkadot/node/core/pvf/common/src/worker/mod.rs`: unit tests\
    \ for `check_security_status` against existing/missing worker dirs (the \"existing\
    \ dir\" case runs on a thread with a larger stack, since the Linux `clone(2)`\
    \ probe needs more than the default `cargo test` thread stack).\n  - `polkadot/node/core/pvf/tests/it/security_checks.rs`:\
    \ new integration test file exercising `--check-security-features` against the\
    \ real `prepare-worker`/`execute-worker` binaries.\n\n# Checklist\n\n* [x] My\
    \ PR includes a detailed description as outlined in the \"Description\" and its\
    \ two subsections above.\n* [ ] My PR follows the [labeling requirements](\nhttps://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/blob/master/docs/contributor/CONTRIBUTING.md#Process\n\
    ) of this project (at minimum one label for `T` required)\n    * External contributors:\
    \ Use `/cmd label <label-name>` to add labels\n    * Maintainers can also add\
    \ labels manually\n* [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\
    \ (if applicable)\n* [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or\
    \ that my feature works (if applicable)"
crates:
- name: polkadot
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-cli
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-node-core-pvf
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-node-core-pvf-common
  bump: minor
